@startuml
title From a derived to a hand-written Packable, and what stays the same
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
}

start
:Struct with sub-Field members
{ bool, bool, FieldCompressedString }
derived Packable: N = 3;
:1. Bit widths: 1 + 1 bits share a Field,
   the string is already exactly one Field
   (total per Field <= 253 bits);
:2. pack(): flags = default | redeemed << 1
   [flags as Field, rating field]  -> N = 2;
:3. unpack(): cast to u64, test each bit,
   rebuild the string from its Field;
:4. Round-trip test: all four flag combinations,
   each flag alone shows disjoint bits;
if (Is the struct read on a private hot path?) then (yes)
  :Measure with aztec profile gates
  before and after;<<#FDEEEE>>
  note right
    Measured once: a two-bool
    pack cost +7 gates on a
    private DelayedPublicMutable
    read. Public saving still real.
  end note
else (no)
  :Public write / read only:
  the saving is N slots, no circuit cost;
endif
if (Is a contract already deployed?) then (yes)
  :Schedule with a storage break:
  every slot after the struct moves,
  notes under moved slots are unspendable;<<#FDEEEE>>
else (no)
  :Ship it: layout is free to change
  until the first deployment;
endif
:ABI unchanged: setter takes 3 fields,
getter returns 3 fields, TypeScript untouched;
stop
@enduml
